# P4 REVISION v1.x - the Tab5 as it has shipped from the factory so far
# (M5_CHIP=v1, the default). Added on top of sdkconfig.defaults by the root
# CMakeLists.txt.
#
# The Tab5's P4 is an engineering sample, a revision BEFORE 3.0. The IDF's
# own Kconfig warns: "Revisions higher than 3.0 (included) and revisions less
# than 3.0 have huge hardware difference."
#
# Without these keys the IDF assumes rev >= 3.01 and a 400MHz CPU (its
# default), and the SECOND-STAGE BOOTLOADER DOES NOT RUN: the ROM loads the
# segments, jumps to the entry point, and the very first instruction is
# already illegal (MTVAL=0x0), followed by a watchdog reset in an infinite
# loop. No app log shows up at all - it never runs.
#
# The Arduino framework gets this right on its own because its board JSON
# declares "chip_variant": "esp32p4_es" and it uses the precompiled sdkconfig
# from framework-arduinoespressif32-libs/esp32p4_es (REV_MIN_FULL=1, CPU
# 360MHz). With framework = espidf that chip_variant is IGNORED - here we
# have to declare it ourselves.
CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=y
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_1=y
CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_360=y
